{% set local_problem %}
<p>New Hope properties often sit among mature trees — oaks, pines, and hardwoods that drop debris constantly. Without protection, that debris fills gutters, creates clogs, and causes overflow that damages your home.</p>

<p>Cleaning gutters on wooded properties is a never-ending battle. Pine needles fall year-round. Leaves come in fall. Every heavy storm brings more debris. Gutter guards break this cycle by keeping debris out while letting water through.</p>

<p>For New Hope homeowners tired of the ladder or tired of paying for repeated cleanings, guards are a permanent solution.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers or screens that fit over or inside your gutters. They allow water in while blocking leaves, pine needles, and debris. Different types work better for different challenges.</p>

<p>For New Hope's wooded properties, we often recommend micro-mesh guards. Unlike basic screens, micro-mesh blocks fine debris like pine needles and shingle grit while still handling heavy water flow.</p>

<p>We'll assess your specific situation — tree types, debris volume, existing gutters — and recommend the best solution.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed gutter guards throughout eastern Madison County for over 20 years. We know New Hope's tree coverage is heavy and select products accordingly.</p>

